      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Endodontic diagnosis and treatment can range from simple to extremely complex. But no matter how simple a case may seem, a thorough examination by the treating endodontist is imperative before any treatment is done. Taking the time to perform an examination in a consistent and methodical approach can rescue the patient from unnecessary treatment, and the treating dentist from potential liability. The patient may be frustrated from repeating many of the same tests performed by the referring dentist, but this situation can be resolved with clear communication from the general dentist and the endodontist as to the benefits of the endodontist's exam. With proper communication, patients will recognize that their general dentist and endodontist are concerned that they receive the best of care."},
